<h2>Asobi Review 1.0 (build 1837) <span class="when">Oct 26, 2026</span></h2>
<ul>
<li>Improvements and fixes.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<div class="earlier">Earlier updates</div>
<h3>1.0 (build 1833) <span class="when">Oct 26, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li>Improvements and fixes.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1830) <span class="when">Oct 26, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li>Improvements and fixes.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1827) <span class="when">Oct 24, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li>Improvements and fixes.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1824) <span class="when">Oct 24, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Reviews in Open Recent</b>: every review you share is listed under its name, and choosing it reopens the review, as Reopen in the Review Manager does. Switching optimized media on or off no longer adds the clip on screen to the list.</li>
<li><b>Save and Save As, plainly</b>: both write the session (.otio). Save writes to the file the session came from; Save As asks for a name and place. The playlist&#8217;s Export Timeline is now Save As too.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1820) <span class="when">Oct 24, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Save works with several windows open</b>: each window keeps its own saved state, so Save in one is no longer undone by another, and quitting asks only about the windows that really have unsaved changes, by name.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1816) <span class="when">Oct 24, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>A tidier playlist</b>: drag a row by its &#10303; grip, use the larger up and down arrows, or right-click for Move to Top and Move to Bottom; the drop line now shows at the top of the list too. A click on a thumbnail plays that clip.</li>
<li><b>Compare pairs, simpler</b>: pick a clip from the row&#8217;s compare menu (the shot&#8217;s other versions first) or drop one clip onto another, and B sits under A as a &#8220;vs&#8221; row that moves and plays with it. Comments brought in from Kitsu no longer make B play on its own too.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1807) <span class="when">Oct 23, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Zoom flip fixed</b>: Flip for Everyone When Zoomed In no longer gets stuck on the source or bounces between the preview and the source (the color flicker). It switches at the review copy&#8217;s 1:1 both ways.</li>
<li><b>Flips are warmed up</b>: parked on a clip with a source, Asobi opens the source and decodes the frame you&#8217;re on in the background, so a flip shows it at once.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
